  "requests": [
    {
      "id": "moss-atlas-request-01",
      "ordinal": 1,
      "kind": "initial",
      "text": "Use moldea to create a standalone Agent Skill named moss-labels under skills/moss-labels/ for Moss Atlas, a fictional volunteer herbarium. It should turn supplied specimen notes into consistent accession-label text without inventing taxonomy or collection facts. Labels currently use an MA- prefix followed by four digits. Include SKILL.md and a small reference file with grounded examples and a missing-data example. Keep this deliverable to the skill artifact and its examples.\n",
      "sessionId": "01a1367e-298f-7da2-a3d5-620ba00d6f46",
      "eventOrdinal": 8,
      "beforeCommit": "9ed705a7294bc483dcae9a408984c9b5262b1f43",
      "afterCommit": "7281bdba4dd0d9b6b03c0f8f0ce3e3838ab112ec",
      "observedResult": "Created the two-file standalone moss-labels skill with grounded examples and missing-data handling. Used the independent Agent Skill route without moldea initialization, CLI/gate calls or canonical state. Structural validation passed; the actor also reported an informal five-case host sub-agent check, whose encrypted prompt is explicitly redacted and whose separate internal history is outside the parent recording.",
      "redactionIds": []
    },
    {
      "id": "moss-atlas-request-02",
      "ordinal": 2,
      "kind": "follow-up",
      "text": "Add a standalone tools/sort-volunteers.mjs utility that reads a JSON array of volunteer names from stdin and writes the names as a JSON array sorted alphabetically without regard to case. Preserve input order for names that compare equally. An empty array is valid; malformed JSON, non-array input or non-string names should fail with a concise stderr message and nonzero exit code. Include focused subprocess tests runnable with node --test tools/sort-volunteers.test.mjs. It needs no application imports or npm script.\n",
      "sessionId": "01a1367e-298f-7da2-a3d5-620ba00d6f46",
      "eventOrdinal": 94,
      "beforeCommit": "7281bdba4dd0d9b6b03c0f8f0ce3e3838ab112ec",
      "afterCommit": "4a05ff1238ed92a313a96932e5787056385d5972",
      "observedResult": "Added a standalone stable, case-insensitive volunteer-name sorter and 18 passing subprocess tests. Only the two tools files changed. The project remained unadopted, and the actor made no moldea gate/CLI/canonical calls or announcements.",
      "redactionIds": []
    },
    {
      "id": "moss-atlas-request-03",
      "ordinal": 3,
      "kind": "follow-up",
      "text": "Moss Atlas has adopted MOSS- followed by five digits as the accession format, effective now. Please update the standalone skill and examples for that format. Keep all supplied specimen facts and uncertainty grounded, and continue to flag invalid accessions instead of inventing or padding them.\n",
      "sessionId": "01a1367e-298f-7da2-a3d5-620ba00d6f46",
      "eventOrdinal": 136,
      "beforeCommit": "4a05ff1238ed92a313a96932e5787056385d5972",
      "afterCommit": "313600a600e4660737efb5ed38d7a795b67e7f50",
      "observedResult": "Updated the standalone skill and grounded examples to MOSS- plus five digits, preserving other specimen facts and uncertainty. Structural validation and fixture comparison passed. A second helper reported six informal cases; parent assertions check helper-produced response artifacts rather than independently demonstrating application/model executions. Extra historical-format/conversion prose was simplified in the next recorded intervention.",
      "redactionIds": []
    },
    {
      "id": "moss-atlas-request-04",
      "ordinal": 4,
      "kind": "intervention",
      "text": "Please keep the skill and examples focused on the current MOSS format. Remove the extra historical-format and conversion paragraphs; the general invalid-accession rule already covers nonmatching input. Preserve the current regex, grounded fixture values, missing-data handling and all specimen-fact safeguards.\n",
      "sessionId": "01a1367e-298f-7da2-a3d5-620ba00d6f46",
      "eventOrdinal": 201,
      "beforeCommit": "313600a600e4660737efb5ed38d7a795b67e7f50",
      "afterCommit": "414825f50fb2d9ee748a9b9bd3961d172d2f04bd",
      "observedResult": "Applied the recorded driver editorial intervention: removed historical-format/conversion paragraphs while preserving the current MOSS regex, grounded fixture values, missing-data handling and factual safeguards. Structural validation passed; no foundation or CLI/Core was introduced.",
      "redactionIds": []
    },
    {
      "id": "moss-atlas-request-05",
      "ordinal": 5,
      "kind": "follow-up",
      "text": "Write a short tools/README.md for the volunteer-name sorter, covering its JSON input/output, case-insensitive alphabetical comparison, stable equal-name order and error behavior. Include small copyable examples that you check against the utility, including an empty list. Keep this to the standalone sorter documentation.\n",
      "sessionId": "01a1367e-298f-7da2-a3d5-620ba00d6f46",
      "eventOrdinal": 240,
      "beforeCommit": "414825f50fb2d9ee748a9b9bd3961d172d2f04bd",
